# swiggy-instamart-portal — environment. COPY to .env and fill in locally.
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a real value (G6).
#
# This CLI NEVER logs in and NEVER refreshes (G9): the ozone refresh token is
# single-use, and rotating it breaks the live session belonging to JIVO's e-com
# team AND the production keepalive cron. It only CONSUMES a session a human (or
# JIVO's existing automation) already established.

# Where the inherited session lives. Defaults to
#   ~/.config/swiggy-instamart-cli/config.json
# which is the file JIVO's existing swiggy-instamart-cli already maintains.
#SWIGGY_CONFIG=/path/to/config.json

# Or supply the tokens directly (env always wins over the config file).
#   SWIGGY_TOKEN        -> ads/brand lane, sent as `authorization: Bearer <jwt>`
#   SWIGGY_SUPPLY_TOKEN -> vendor lane, sent as `Abacus-Token: <jwt>`
# Note the vendor lane on picker.swiggy.com uses a DIFFERENT header name.
#SWIGGY_TOKEN=
#SWIGGY_SUPPLY_TOKEN=

# The request-signing pepper: a 32-char constant embedded in Swiggy's
# media_loader.wasm. It is a SECRET and is deliberately absent from this repo.
# Without it, calls to brand-portal-service-http cannot be signed and will 403.
# JIVO's copy lives in ~/ecomcliauto/swiggy/signer/ — read it from there, do not
# paste it into a tracked file.
#SWIGGY_SIGN_PEPPER=

# app_version is server-validated and has moved over time (1.4.122 -> 0.0.32 ->
# 0.0.34 observed). A stale value returns 403 "App version update required", so
# read it from the live page shell rather than trusting this default.
#SWIGGY_APP_VERSION=0.0.34
